   "text": {
    "L1": "Equivalent fractions name the same amount of the same whole.",
    "L2": "A fraction can have more pieces without being more. Let us fold one half again.",
    "L3": "The two halves become four equal pieces, and the shaded half becomes two quarters.",
    "L4": "So one half and two quarters are equal, even though two has more pieces than one.",
    "L5": "To make an equivalent fraction, multiply the top and bottom by the same number.",
    "L6": "For example, five becomes ten when we multiply by two, so three fifths becomes six tenths.",
    "L7": "Adding the same number is different. One half does not become two thirds.",
    "L8": "Now tap the fraction that shows one half using four equal parts."
   },
